exit|way-out|NOUN|Way out|A door, opening or route through which someone can leave a place.|lối ra|A green sign marks the exit beside the ticket counter.|Một biển màu xanh lá đánh dấu lối ra bên cạnh quầy vé.|Countable; an emergency exit, the nearest exit. Entrance names a way in.|0
exit|leave-a-place|VERB|Leave a place|To go out of a room, building or other place.|ra khỏi; đi ra|The actors exited the hall through a side door.|Các diễn viên ra khỏi hội trường qua một cửa bên.|Transitive exit a building or intransitive exit through a door; often formal or used in instructions.|1
exit|close-a-program|VERB|Close a program|To stop using and close a computer program or leave its current operating mode.|thoát chương trình|Save your drawing before you exit the application.|Hãy lưu bản vẽ trước khi bạn thoát ứng dụng.|Exit a program or application. Saving is a separate action and is not implied by exit.|2
mist|fine-airborne-droplets|NOUN|Fine airborne water droplets|Tiny water droplets suspended in the air that make the surroundings less clear.|sương mù nhẹ|Mist covered the pond at sunrise, but the far bank was still visible.|Sương mù nhẹ phủ mặt ao lúc mặt trời mọc, nhưng vẫn nhìn thấy bờ bên kia.|Usually uncountable; a layer of mist, morning mist. Generally lighter than thick fog.|-
raisin|dried-grape|NOUN|Dried grape|A grape that has been dried and is eaten as a sweet food.|nho khô|She added a handful of raisins to the oat biscuits.|Cô ấy thêm một nắm nho khô vào bánh quy yến mạch.|Countable; a raisin, raisins. Raisin names the dried fruit, not a fresh grape variety.|-
ton|large-weight-unit|NOUN|Large unit of weight|A unit used for heavy loads, with different values in different measurement systems.|tấn theo hệ đo được dùng|The cargo record listed the weight in tons but did not specify the measurement system.|Hồ sơ hàng hóa ghi khối lượng theo đơn vị tấn nhưng không nêu hệ đo.|Countable; two tons. Distinguish the US short ton, imperial long ton and metric tonne when precision matters.|0
wicked|morally-bad|ADJECTIVE|Morally bad|Deliberately cruel or morally very wrong.|độc ác; xấu xa|The story's wicked ruler imprisoned anyone who questioned his orders.|Kẻ cai trị độc ác trong câu chuyện bỏ tù bất cứ ai chất vấn mệnh lệnh của hắn.|Often used in stories or strong moral judgments; wickedly and wickedness are related forms.|-
